    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1274">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1247" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/4–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-24T19:00:00+08:00">April 24, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 24—7:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1327. Admiral Badger in conversation this afternoon said that he was studying
                    possibility of modified emergency evacuation plan which would provide protection
                    for civilians essentially as contemplated (mytel 1319).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
